WEBVTT

NOTE
Transcribed from the narration in this video. Every figure the
speaker states matches the OECD time-use data behind this page.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.300
Bonjour! You want to
know how my day goes?

2
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:04.560
Sit down. There's no rush here.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.660
I wake up and I take my time.

4
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.580
Breakfast, a warm croissant,
butter, good coffee.

5
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.780
In France, we spend 12 hours and 32
minutes a day, just on personal care.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.220
We believe the body
deserves attention.

7
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:20.680
Then I work, but not like crazy.

8
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:24.620
I do about 3 hours and 24
minutes of paid work a day.

9
00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:28.020
We work around 1,487 hours a year.

10
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.380
Enough to live, not
enough to forget how to.

11
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.800
After that, there's
the invisible work.

12
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.100
Cooking a real meal, tidying up,
maybe helping a neighbour.

13
00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.680
And then, leisure.

14
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.920
Almost 5 hours of it.

15
00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:46.480
I read, I walk, I sit at a café and
watch people argue about cheese.

16
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.040
4 hours and 53 minutes,
every single day.

17
00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.740
Oh, and the best part?

18
00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:53.880
Most of us retire by 61.

19
00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:57.100
You see, in France,
the day is not a race.

20
00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.620
It's a meal, and we
take every course.
